Next.js SSR + OpenCode SDK integration gotcha: createClient() from @opencode-vibe/core relies on multiServerSSE singleton which only exists in browser context. In SSR (Server Components), you MUST use createClientSSR() instead, which fetches from /api/opencode-servers and constructs proxy URLs (http://localhost:8423/api/opencode/${port}). 

Root cause: After extraction to @opencode-vibe/core, the multiServerSSE singleton is browser-only. SSR code can't access client-side singletons - it needs async discovery via fetch().

Fix pattern:
```ts
// ❌ SSR - FAILS with ECONNREFUSED
